"rationale": "The district's Republican lean and a broad Lean R expert consensus anchor the forecast, but the open seat, Flippo's ethics headlines, the incumbent's public break with him, and a Democratic-leaning polling picture in a favorable environment keep this well short of safe. Markets price Flippo near two-to-one, consistent with a modest Republican edge.", "watch": "Any late poll, a shift in the Chapman spoiler dynamic, or further fallout from the donation reports could move this toward a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 60 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Open seat: Mark Amodei (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Northern Nevada's open House seat is the rare Republican-held district that Democrats see as a pickup chance this cycle. The seat leans Republican by about seven points, but the national environment favors Democrats, and the Republican nominee, David Flippo, has spent the closing weeks answering reports about donations credited to deceased individuals and a more serious firing record than he acknowledged. Mark Amodei, the retiring incumbent, has declined to back his party's replacement, and the Washoe County GOP has distanced itself from him.\n\nDemocrats are also boosting independent Lynn Chapman, who may siphon votes in a close race. Polling is sparse and months old, showing a near-even race, while forecasters mostly call it Lean Republican and markets give Flippo roughly a two-thirds chance. The expectation is a narrow Republican win with real downside risk.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.213, "margin": -4.52}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2977, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2868, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2952, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2127, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2908, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3379, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_d